{
  "source": "<!-- document-source {\"page\":4,\"block\":\"p4-gazer-statblock\",\"method\":\"native-pdf-text\",\"confidence\":1,\"bbox\":{\"x\":53,\"y\":44,\"width\":243,\"height\":518}} -->\n# Gazer\n\nGAZER CR 1/2\nA tiny, toothed eye weaves through the air, its halo of\nworming eyestalks vigilant for threats.\nAC 13 (Natural Armor) Initiative +2 (12)\nHP 13 (3d4 + 6) Size Tiny (8 in. diameter)\nSpeed Fly 30 ft. (Hover) Type Aberration (Beholder)\nMOD SAVE MOD SAVE MOD SAVE\nSTR 10 +0 +0 DEX 14 +2 +2 CON 15 +2 +2\nINT 15 +2 +2 WIS 15 +2 +2 CHA 13 +1 +1\nSkills Perception +4, Stealth +4\nImmunities Prone\nSenses Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 14\nLanguages Can crudely mimic any language it has heard\nXP 100 Proficiency Bonus +2\nTraits\nFlighty Familiar. An Incapacitated gazer subjected to the\nFind Familiar ritual is transformed into a familiar spirit.\nIt obeys the caster’s commands until it fails an\nIntelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma Saving Throw, at\nwhich point it becomes hostile once more.\nSpying Eye. Each beholder in a 5-mile Emanation from the\ngazer can perceive the world through the gazer’s senses.\nActions\nEye Rays. The gazer shoots two of the following magical\neye rays at random (reroll duplicates), choosing targets it\ncan see within 60 feet:\n1. Dazing Ray. The target must make a WISDOM SAVING\nTHROW: DC 12. FAILURE: The creature is Charmed and\nDazed until the end of its next turn.\n2. Fear Ray. The target must make a WISDOM SAVING THROW:\nDC 12. FAILURE: The creature is Frightened until the end\nof its next turn.\n3. Frost Ray. The target must make a\nDEXTERITY SAVING THROW: DC 12. FAILURE: 10 (3d6) Cold\ndamage.\n4. Force Ray. The target must make a\nSTRENGTH SAVING THROW: DC 12. FAILURE: The target is\npushed 25 (1d10 x 5) feet away from the gazer.\n",
